ation requires:\\n1. Activating the neighbor\\n2. Enabling community sending\\n3. Entering the L2VPN address family context\\n\\nThe complete equivalent configuration would also require the base BGP configuration (AS number, neighbor definitions) which isn't shown in the translation scope.\", 'trans_template': 'address-family l2vpn vpls'}]]": 1,
    "['local-address [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp [AS_NUMBER]', 'parent_command': ['vpdn-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'vpdn-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp [AS_NUMBER]\\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 update-source Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command assumes you've already configured the BGP process with `router bgp [AS_NUMBER]`\\n2. The Juniper `local-address 1.1.1.1` maps to Cisco's `update-source` pointing to the loopback interface that has the 1.1.1.1 address\\n3. The neighbor address (2.2.2.2) is included from the subsequent `neighbor` command in the Juniper config for context\\n4. In Cisco, you typically specify the interface (Loopback0) rather than the IP address directly\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp [AS_NUMBER]'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2 update-source Loopback0', 'parent_command': ['vpdn-group [parameter1]'], 'root': 'vpdn-group [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp [AS_NUMBER]\\n neighbor 2.2.2.2 update-source Loopback0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Cisco command assumes you've already configured the BGP process with `router bgp [AS_NUMBER]`\\n2. The Juniper `local-address 1.1.1.1` maps to Cisco's `update-source` pointing to the loopback interface that has the 1.1.1.1 address\\n3. The neighbor address (2.2.2.2) is included from the subsequent `neighbor` command in the Juniper config for context\\n4. In Cisco, you typically specify the interface (Loopback0) rather than the IP address directly\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 2.2.2.2 update-source Loopback0'}]]": 1,
